-- title:
--   Lemma 2.1, read for every n ⩾ 1, fails — the lazy version ½δ_id + ½μ of any measure meeting its hypotheses meets them too, but no c > 0 has v(R_n) ⩾ exp(cn) for all n ⩾ 1
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a group generated by a finite set $S$, and let $\mu$ be a probability on $\Gamma$ (`IsProbability`) of finite entropy (`HasFiniteEntropy`) whose Poisson boundary is non-trivial (`HasNontrivialPoissonBoundary`): the hypotheses of Lemma 2.1. Let $\nu = \frac12\delta_{id} + \frac12\mu$, its lazy version (the hypothesis `hν`), and define $\varrho_n$ and $\phi$ from $\nu$ as in Lemma 2.1:
--   $$\varrho_n = \inf\{r > 0 : \nu(\{g : |g| \ge r\}) < 1/n\}, \qquad \phi(r) = \sum_{g : |g| \le r} |g|\,\nu(g).$$
--   Then $\nu$ is a probability of finite entropy whose Poisson boundary is non-trivial, and there is no $c > 0$ with $v_{\Gamma,S}(n\,\phi(\varrho_n)) \ge e^{cn}$ for every $n \ge 1$. The statement requires decidable equality on $\Gamma$ (`DecidableEq`) to write the point mass at the identity as an `if`; it is not a further hypothesis on the group.
--
--   Erschler and Zheng, p. 10, Lemma 2.1: “Let $\Gamma$ be a finitely generated group and $|\cdot| = l_S$ a word distance on $\Gamma$. Suppose $\Gamma$ admits a probability measure $\mu$ of finite entropy such that the Poisson boundary $(\Gamma, \mu)$ is nontrivial. Let $\varrho_n = \inf\{r > 0 : \mu(\{g : |g| \geqslant r\}) < 1/n\}$ and $\phi(r) = \sum_{g : |g| \leqslant r} |g|\mu(g)$. Then there exists a constant $c = c(\Gamma, \mu) > 0$ such that $v_{\Gamma,S}(R_n) \geqslant \exp(cn)$ where $R_n = n\phi(\varrho_n)$.”
--
--   The printed sentence gives no range for $n$. Read as every $n \ge 1$, it is false whenever its hypotheses can be met at all, and this statement shows it: applied to $\nu$, that reading would give $c > 0$ with $e^{cn} \le v_{\Gamma,S}(R_n)$ for every $n \ge 1$, which the statement rules out. The proof of the lemma concludes the bound “for all $n$ sufficiently large” (p. 11), which is the milestone `ErschlerZheng.exp_le_growth_of_hasNontrivialPoissonBoundary`.
-- source:
--   Erschler, A. and Zheng, T., Growth of periodic Grigorchuk groups, Invent. Math. 219 (2020) 1069–1155, https://doi.org/10.1007/s00222-019-00922-0 (arXiv:1802.09077v2, whose page numbers are used), p. 10, Lemma 2.1 read for every n (fails for the lazy measure; the paper concludes it for all n sufficiently large)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ErschlerZheng_Walks

namespace ErschlerZheng

theorem lazy_hasNontrivialPoissonBoundary_and_not_exists_forall_exp_le_growth {Γ : Type*}
    [Group Γ] [DecidableEq Γ] (S : Finset Γ) (hS : Subgroup.closure (S : Set Γ) = ⊤) (μ : Γ → ℝ)
    (hμ : IsProbability μ) (hH : HasFiniteEntropy μ) (hP : HasNontrivialPoissonBoundary μ)
    (ν : Γ → ℝ) (hν : ∀ g, ν g = (if g = 1 then 1 / 2 else 0) + μ g / 2)
    (ϱ : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hϱ : ∀ n : ℕ, ϱ n =
      sInf {r : ℝ | 0 < r ∧ mass ν {g | r ≤ (wordLength (S : Set Γ) g : ℝ)} < 1 / n})
    (φ : ℝ → ℝ)
    (hφ : ∀ r : ℝ, φ r = ∑' g : ball (S : Set Γ) r, (wordLength (S : Set Γ) g : ℝ) * ν g) :
    IsProbability ν ∧ HasFiniteEntropy ν ∧ HasNontrivialPoissonBoundary ν ∧
      ¬ ∃ c > 0, ∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n → Real.exp (c * n) ≤ growth (S : Set Γ) (n * φ (ϱ n)) := by
  sorry

end ErschlerZheng
